  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Clear Signal",
    "overview": "The library makes every state as easy to see as it is for assistive technology to announce. If a screen reader hears \"selected\", \"invalid\", \"expanded\" or \"focused\", a sighted user sees it too, without relying on colour alone. State changes show up as thick borders, a solid ring, a lift or an underline, never as a faint tint. This is a component library rather than a brand: it inherits the host's fonts, takes the host's palette through `--color-primary-*`, `--color-secondary-*` and `--color-neutral-*` ramps, and adds a small set of strong defaults that look right in the Accessible Astro Starter and stay neutral anywhere else.\n\nDensity is moderate and touch-friendly. Interactive targets stay at or above 2.75rem (44px) where the layout allows. Spacing and type both use fluid `clamp()` scales, so components grow with the viewport and need no breakpoint overrides. Light and dark themes come from `light-dark()` on every color token. Components never branch on a `.darkmode` class for color.\n\nStyles are written to be overridden. Every component selector is wrapped in `:where()` for zero specificity, so a consumer's single class beats the library. Motion is decorative and opt-in. Anything that moves sits behind `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`, and the reduced-motion fallback stays visible but still.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Explicit states: border, ring, lift or underline. A state is never shown by color alone.",
      "Bordered rather than shadowed: 2px borders define surfaces, and shadows are reserved for floating layers.",
      "Semantic color triplets (`border` / `bg` / `text`) for default, info, success, warning, error, primary and secondary.",
      "Fluid tokens for space and type. No hard-coded rem values inside components.",
      "Zero-specificity styles with `:where()`, so consumers can theme without fighting the library.",
      "Logical properties throughout (`inline-size`, `padding-block`, `inset-inline-start`)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Triplet Rule",
        "body": "A colored component sets all three colors of a single triplet (`--color-X-border`, `--color-X-bg`, `--color-X-text`). Never mix the border from one meaning with the background from another, and never hard-code an `hsl()` that duplicates a token.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token-or-Fallback Rule",
        "body": "Components read color only through `var(--color-…)`. A component that needs a value the system lacks reads a consumer ramp with an inline fallback (`var(--color-neutral-200, hsl(…))`). It never defines a bare literal.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Not-Color-Alone Rule",
        "body": "Every color-coded state also has a non-color signal: an icon, border weight, underline, ring or text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Scale-Only Rule",
        "body": "Font sizes inside components come from `--font-size-*`. A literal `1.25rem` or `0.875rem` is a deviation.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Underline-Is-Interactive Rule",
        "body": "Underlines mean \"this is actionable\". Hover and focus move the underline closer (`text-underline-offset` 4px → 2px) instead of adding or removing it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Space-Token Rule",
        "body": "Padding, margin, gap and inset values inside components come from `--space-*`. Literal rem values are deviations, except geometric sizes such as icon boxes and 2.75rem touch targets.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-Until-Floating Rule",
        "body": "Inline surfaces (cards, tabs, notifications, inputs) never carry a resting shadow. Only detached layers use `--elevation-*`, and always through the token.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Radius Rule",
        "body": "A surface uses `--radius-m` and a control inside it uses `--radius-s`. Never write `0.5rem` or `0.25rem` literally.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** wrap every component selector in `:where()` so consumer classes win without `!important`.",
      "**Do** read color only through `--color-{meaning}-{border|bg|text}`, and give fallbacks when reading the host's `--color-neutral-*` / `--color-primary-*` ramps.",
      "**Do** use `--space-*` for padding, gaps and offsets, and `--font-size-*` for type.",
      "**Do** use `--radius-m` on surfaces and `--radius-s` on controls.",
      "**Do** use `--animation-timing` for easing. Durations are 0.2s for state changes and 0.3s for disclosure and image transitions.",
      "**Do** put every transition and keyframe behind `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`.",
      "**Do** keep interactive targets at least 2.75rem (44px) in both dimensions where layout allows.",
      "**Do** use logical properties (`border-inline-start`, `border-start-start-radius`, `padding-block`)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** hard-code `hsl()`, `rgb()` or hex values in a component when a token exists. In particular, don't use `light-dark(hsl(0 0% 10%), hsl(0 0% 90%))` for borders; use `--color-default-border`.",
      "**Don't** redeclare `--transition-easing: cubic-bezier(0.165, 0.84, 0.44, 1)` locally. That is `--animation-timing`.",
      "**Don't** read tokens the library doesn't define (`--cubic-bezier`, `--animation-speed-*`) without also defining them or giving a fallback that matches the library's own tokens.",
      "**Don't** add resting shadows to inline surfaces. Shadows are for floating layers.",
      "**Don't** remove `outline` on focus unless the ring replaces it with equal or greater visibility.",
      "**Don't** use physical properties (`border-left`, `border-top-left-radius`) in component CSS.",
      "**Don't** signal state by color alone."
    ]
  }
}
